---
import Studio from "../../layouts/Studio.astro";
import RelatedPosts from "../../components/RelatedPosts.astro";
import { SITE, DEFAULT_OG, fmtDate, iso, POSTS } from "../../lib/blog.mjs";

const slug = "the-real-cost-of-renting-your-storefront";
const idx = POSTS.findIndex((p) => p.slug === slug);
const post = POSTS[idx];

const canonical = `${SITE}/blog/${slug}/`;
const ogImage = post.coverImage ? `${SITE}${post.coverImage}` : DEFAULT_OG;
const primaryTag = post.tags[0] || "Notes";
const readMins = post.readMins;
const showUpdated = post.updatedDate && +new Date(post.updatedDate) > +new Date(post.pubDate);
const updatedLabel = showUpdated ? `Updated ${fmtDate(post.updatedDate)}` : null;

const jsonld = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BlogPosting",
      "@id": `${canonical}#post`,
      headline: post.title,
      description: post.description,
      datePublished: iso(post.pubDate),
      dateModified: iso(post.updatedDate || post.pubDate),
      author: { "@type": "Person", name: "Divyansh Sood", url: `${SITE}/`, "@id": `${SITE}/#person` },
      publisher: {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "@id": `${SITE}/#studio`,
        name: "Divyansh Sood® Studio",
        logo: { "@type": "ImageObject", url: `${SITE}/icon.svg` },
      },
      isPartOf: { "@type": "WebSite", "@id": `${SITE}/#website` },
      mainEntityOfPage: { "@type": "WebPage", "@id": canonical },
      image: ogImage,
      articleSection: primaryTag,
      keywords: post.tags.join(", "),
      wordCount: 725,
      timeRequired: `PT${readMins}M`,
      speakable: {
        "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
        cssSelector: [".post-title", ".post-lead"],
      },
      inLanguage: "en",
      url: canonical,
    },
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: `${SITE}/` },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Blog", item: `${SITE}/blog/` },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: post.title, item: canonical },
      ],
    },
  ],
});
---

<Studio
  title={post.seoTitle ?? `${post.title} · Divyansh Sood`}
  description={post.description}
  canonical={canonical}
  keywords={post.tags.join(", ")}
  ogType="article"
  ogTitle={post.title}
  ogImage={ogImage}
  ogImageW={1200}
  ogImageH={750}
  articlePublished={iso(post.pubDate)}
  articleModified={iso(post.updatedDate || post.pubDate)}
  tags={post.tags}
  jsonld={jsonld}
>
  <main>
    <header class="post-hero">
      <div class="post-hero-bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="wrap narrow">
        <div class="eyebrow">
          <span>{primaryTag}</span>
          <span>{fmtDate(post.pubDate)}</span>
          {updatedLabel && <span class="post-updated">{updatedLabel}</span>}
          <span>{readMins} min read</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="post-title">{post.title}</h1>
        <p class="post-lead">{post.description}</p>
        <div class="post-meta">
          <span>By Divyansh Sood</span><span>{fmtDate(post.pubDate)}</span><span>{readMins} min read</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    {post.coverImage && (
      <div class="wrap narrow">
        <figure class="post-cover">
          <img src={post.coverImage} alt={post.title} width="1200" height="750" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" />
        </figure>
      </div>
    )}

    <article class="wrap narrow post-body">
      <p>The most expensive word in your tech stack is <em>monthly</em>.</p>
<p>Not because any single bill is large. Because monthly costs hide. ₹2,599 here, ₹999 there, an app at ₹1,500 — none of it triggers the part of your brain that resists a big number. So it never gets questioned. And it compounds for as long as you’re in business.</p>
<p>Let me make the invisible visible.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id="what-youre-actually-renting">What you’re actually renting</h2>
<p>When your store runs on a hosted builder plus apps, you’re renting four separate things:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>The platform</strong> — the right to keep your store online</li>
<li><strong>The features</strong> — apps for reviews, bundles, fields, upsells, popups</li>
<li><strong>The theme</strong> — sometimes one-time, often subscription for updates</li>
<li><strong>The lock-in</strong> — the cost, in time and risk, of ever leaving</li>
</ol>
<p>The first three show up on a card statement. The fourth is the one that actually traps you, and it never appears on any invoice.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id="the-three-year-math">The three-year math</h2>
<p>Here’s a realistic mid-tier setup for a growing D2C brand:</p>



































<table><thead><tr><th>Line item</th><th>Monthly</th><th>3-year total</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Platform plan</td><td>₹2,600</td><td>₹93,600</td></tr><tr><td>6 apps (avg ₹1,200 each)</td><td>₹7,200</td><td>₹2,59,200</td></tr><tr><td>Premium theme updates</td><td>₹400</td><td>₹14,400</td></tr><tr><td>Transaction fees (beyond gateway)</td><td>varies</td><td>₹50,000+</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Total</strong></td><td><strong>~₹10,200</strong></td><td><strong>~₹4,17,000</strong></td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>Four lakh rupees over three years — and at the end of it, you own nothing. Stop paying and the store goes dark. You can’t take the theme, the app logic, or the custom fields with you.</p>
<p>A custom-coded storefront inverts this. You pay once to build, then hosting is ₹0–₹6,000/year because a custom site is just files on a fast CDN. The asset is yours. There’s no monthly feature rent because the features are in your code.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id="but-i-dont-have-the-build-budget">”But I don’t have the build budget”</h2>
<p>Fair. This is the real tension, so let me be honest about it.</p>
<p>If you’re pre-revenue or still finding product-market fit, <strong>rent.</strong> Speed and flexibility are worth more than ownership when you don’t yet know what you’re building. A hosted builder is the correct call.</p>
<p>The mistake is staying in rent mode out of habit once you’re past that. Once you have steady revenue and a brand worth protecting, the monthly stack quietly becomes more expensive than owning — and you keep paying it because the bill is small enough to ignore.</p>
<p>The crossover is usually earlier than founders think. Run your own numbers above. If your three-year rent total is north of ₹3 lakh, a custom build often pays for itself inside 18 months — and then keeps paying.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id="ownership-is-also-leverage">Ownership is also leverage</h2>
<p>The financial case is the obvious one. The strategic case is bigger.</p>
<p>When you own your code:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>No platform can change your business overnight.</strong> No surprise pricing tier, no deprecated app, no “we’re sunsetting this feature.”</li>
<li><strong>You can build the thing nobody else has.</strong> The drop mechanic, the configurator, the loyalty logic — none of it waits on whether an app exists.</li>
<li><strong>You can leave any developer, not any platform.</strong> Custom code is readable by any competent engineer. That’s portability, which is freedom.</li>
</ul>
<p>When we built <a href="https://www.divyanshsood.com/projects/chinkiz/">ChinkiZ Knitting Knife</a> for a 600K-subscriber creator, the whole point was a video gallery and admin panel that no builder offered. Owning the code meant the store could be exactly her, not the nearest template.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id="the-question-to-sit-with">The question to sit with</h2>
<p>Look at your last card statement and add up every recurring charge tied to your store. Multiply by 36.</p>
<p>Then ask: <em>if I’m going to spend that much over three years anyway, would I rather rent something I’ll never own — or own something I’ll never have to rent again?</em></p>
<p>For a brand past validation, the answer is usually obvious the moment you actually do the multiplication.</p>
<hr>
<p><em>I’m Divyansh Sood. I build storefronts that flip the rent-vs-own math inside 18 months for any D2C brand doing meaningful volume. 9 live builds since 2022 — including <a href="https://www.divyanshsood.com/projects/chinkiz/">ChinkiZ Knitting Knife</a>, a 600K-subscriber YouTuber’s creator store built on a video gallery that no template offered.</em></p>
<p><em>If you’ve been quietly watching your monthly stack compound and want a straight quote on what ownership would cost you, <a href="mailto:hello@divyanshsood.com">email me</a> — I’ll send you the math for your actual numbers.</em></p>
      <div class="tags">{post.tags.map((t) => <span>{t}</span>)}</div>
    </article>

    <RelatedPosts slug={slug} audience={post.audience} />

    <section class="post-foot-cta">
      <div class="wrap narrow">
        {post.audience === "indian-smb" ? (
          <>
            <h2>Working on something in India?</h2>
            <p>If a post here matches what you're building, send me the brief. WhatsApp reply in under an hour, 9 AM–9 PM IST — I'll tell you within a day if it's a fit.</p>
            <div class="cta-row">
              <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://wa.me/919816091875" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
                >Message me on WhatsApp <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
              >
              <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/#work">See the work</a>
            </div>
          </>
        ) : post.audience === "d2c-brand" ? (
          <>
            <h2>Building a brand a theme can't carry?</h2>
            <p>If your store has a model that off-the-shelf builders fight — hand-numbered drops, creator commerce, premium D2C — tell me about it. I read every brief personally.</p>
            <div class="cta-row">
              <a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:hello@divyanshsood.com"
                >Email me <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
              >
              <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/#work">See the work</a>
            </div>
          </>
        ) : (
          <>
            <h2>Working on something similar?</h2>
            <p>If a post here matches what you're building, send me the brief. I reply personally, usually within a couple of hours — and I'll tell you within a day if it's a fit.</p>
            <div class="cta-row">
              <a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:hello@divyanshsood.com"
                >Email me <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
              >
              <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://calendly.com/sood-divyansh007/30min" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
                >Book a 15-min intro <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
              >
            </div>
          </>
        )}
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Studio>
